## Why nothing else needs to change (verified)

Everything downstream consumes `indicatorAxis.angle` / `radar.coordToPoint`, and the set of possible angle values is unchanged (still normalized to `[-PI, PI]`), so label/name placement is unaffected:

- `src/component/radar/RadarView.ts:45-58` builds one `AxisBuilder` per indicator with `rotation: indicatorAxis.angle`, `labelDirection: -1`, `tickDirection: -1`, `nameDirection: 1`. `AxisBuilder` derives label/name layout purely from `cfg.rotation` (`src/component/axis/AxisBuilder.ts:850-886`, `:1359`, `:1552`), which is per-axis, not order-dependent.
- `src/component/radar/RadarView.ts:130-173` (polygon split lines/areas) walks indicators in index order and closes the ring; reversing the order only reverses polygon winding, which is irrelevant for the ring-band fill it builds. The `shape: 'circle'` branch (`:99-126`) is angle-independent.
- `src/chart/radar/radarLayout.ts:35-58` and `src/chart/radar/RadarSeries.ts:112`, `:145-146` go through `coordSys.dataToPoint` / `coordToPoint`, which read `indicatorAxis.angle`.
- `src/export/option.ts:22` only re-exports the `RadarOption` type — no edit needed.
- `src/preprocessor/backwardCompat.ts:165-171` maps the deprecated `clockWise` -> `clockwise`, but only for `series.type === 'pie' | 'gauge'`. Radar is a component, not a series option, so leave it alone (unless you deliberately want `radar.clockWise` compat, which upstream does not have).

